body='<p>David Ing’s '+link(P['ocad']['url'],'complete 2026 Understanding Systems pro forma')+' is now available to read. It connects systems inquiry, design, visualisation, and collective learning across twelve modules.</p><p class="note">'+E(P['ocad']['status'])+' The pro forma is published under CC BY by David Ing. The headings, short guides, and inquiry prompts below are editorial aids. Links identify works in the pro forma; inclusion does not mean the atlas has read every linked work.</p><p>'+link('#module-1','Start with module 1')+' · '+link('/learning/isss/','Compare the ISSS modelling bibliography')+' · '+atlas(ocadid,'Inspect the atlas reading-route record')+'</p>'
for m in P['ocad']['modules']:
 body+='<section id="module-'+str(m['number'])+'"><p class="meta">Module '+str(m['number'])+'</p><h2>'+E(m['title'])+'</h2><p>'+E(m['summary'])+'</p><p>'+link(m['source_url'],'Read the corresponding source module')+'</p><p><strong>Editorial inquiry:</strong> '+E(m['exercise'])+'</p>'+details(str(len(m['links']))+' source links in this module','<ul>'+''.join('<li>'+link(l['url'],l['title'] or l['url'])+'</li>' for l in m['links'])+'</ul>')+'</section>'
body+='<section><h2>Read across the course</h2><p>Keep a small record of an inquiry: the situation, your boundary, the people whose accounts differ, the relations you propose, and the observations that might change them. Revisit that record as the methods change. This is an editorial exercise; it is not a claimed course assessment.</p><p>The source’s final section is a placeholder, so this guide adds no final-assessment requirements.</p></section>'
page('/corpora/ing-ocad/','Understanding Systems: a twelve-module reading guide',body)
body='<p>The '+link(P['isss']['url'],'ISSS student resource page')+' is a useful entry into modelling, with software, training leads, and a bibliography spanning several method families. Its emphasis does not define the whole of systems sciences.</p><p class="note">'+E(P['isss']['status'])+' The 57 rows below retain the source’s bibliographic statements, including edition variants. A title appearing twice is not silently treated as two distinct works.</p><section><h2>Choose a route through the sources</h2><p>For feedback over time, start with system dynamics. For heterogeneous actors and local interactions, inspect agent-based models. For relational structure, inspect network methods. Then ask what each representation leaves outside its boundary.</p><p>Compare these modelling routes with '+link('/corpora/ing-ocad/','Ing’s design and inquiry route')+', '+link('/systems-thinking/practice/','the practice laboratory')+', and '+link('/systems-sciences/','the Systems Sciences stewardship page')+'. This comparison is editorial guidance rather than a recommendation attributed to ISSS.</p></section><section><h2>Tools and training leads</h2><p>These are links listed by ISSS. Historical dates, software editions, and access conditions need checking at the destination.</p><ul>'
seen=set()
for r in P['isss']['resources']:
 if r['url'] in seen:continue
 seen.add(r['url']);body+='<li>'+link(r['url'],r['title'] or r['url'])+'</li>'
body+='</ul></section>'
for category in dict.fromkeys(r['category'] for r in P['isss']['readings']):
 rows=[r for r in P['isss']['readings'] if r['category']==category]
 body+='<section><h2>'+E(category)+'</h2><ol>'+''.join('<li>'+E(r['citation'])+(' '+ ' · '.join(link(u,'Source-listed link') for u in r['links']) if r['links'] else '')+'</li>' for r in rows)+'</ol></section>'
body+='<section><h2>Beyond the student list</h2><p>The '+link('https://www.isss.org/home/','ISSS home resource hub')+' links proceedings, a primer, the wiki, and contributed maps and learning accounts. Follow those as separately authored collections.</p><ul>'+''.join('<li>'+link(u,t)+'</li>' for u,t in [('https://journals.isss.org/','ISSS proceedings'),('https://web3.isss.org/primer2/','ISSS primer'),('https://wiki.isss.org/','ISSS wiki'),('https://web3.isss.org/marzolf-aug2023/index.html','Tom Marzolf’s systems learning material'),('https://desc.systems/','Bruce McNaughton’s systems descriptions')])+'</ul></section>'
page('/learning/isss/','ISSS: routes into systems sciences',body)
body='<p>John A Challoner’s '+link('https://rational-understanding.com/researchers/','Rational Understanding researcher modules')+' translate five bodies of work into a common arrangement of definitions and propositions. All five PDFs were read for this guide: 32 pages in total.</p><p class="note">These are secondary reconstructions, version 1 dated 30 September 2026. DG and PG label general definitions and propositions; DS and PS label specialised ones. The modules distinguish explicit claims from reconstructions. Their common format does not prove that the thinkers used the same concepts, and an ISSS header is not by itself evidence of institutional endorsement.</p>'
for m in P['modules']:
 body+='<section id="'+m['id']+'"><h2>'+E(m['title'])+'</h2><p>'+E(m['summary'])+'</p><p><strong>Keep the distinction:</strong> '+E(m['distinction'])+'</p><p>'+link(m['url'],'Read the '+str(m['pages'])+'-page module')+' · '+atlas('publication_u31_'+m['id'],'Inspect the atlas statements')+'</p><ul>'
 for nid,locator,typ,scope in m['concepts']:
  n=next(n for n in d['nodes'] if n['id']==nid);body+='<li>'+atlas(nid,n['label'])+': '+E(locator)+'.</li>'
 body+='</ul></section>'
body+='<section><h2>Compare without collapsing meanings</h2><p>Material openness, energy exchange, and causal openness answer different questions. A system can exchange energy without exchanging matter. Equifinality is conditional; a dissipative structure is not simply anything that changes; organisation can concern relations without supplying a universal management prescription.</p><p><strong>Editorial exercise:</strong> take a proposed organisational claim containing one of these terms. Identify the source proposition, its domain, and the additional argument needed for transfer. Write an observation that would count against that transfer.</p><p>'+link('https://ashby.info/','Read Ashby’s original archive')+'. Original-source checks for the other modules remain part of the research queue; the secondary reading is not reported as their completion.</p></section>'
page('/reading/researcher-modules/','Five researchers, with their distinctions intact',body)
body='<p>Doug Belshaw’s '+link('https://substrate.dougbelshaw.com/orglens-2-making-an-organisational-health-check-people-can-actually-use','second OrgLens development account')+' describes moving from an agent-driven experiment to a fixed reporting pipeline.</p><p>The reported design separates structural checks from model-generated writing. It checks quotations against notes, tests for contradictions, and moves specialist terminology out of the main report. These are claims about the experimental design and its tests.</p><p>The cases were fictional and the readers were simulated. The same AI setup contributed to construction and evaluation, with small samples. Report clarity under those conditions does not establish whether diagnoses are fair or useful to people in a real organisation.</p><p>'+atlas('tool_orglens','Inspect OrgLens and its claimed systems lenses')+' · '+link('https://framagit.org/dynamicskillset/orglens','Read the maintained source repository')+'</p><section><h2>Editorial application: inspect the evidence chain</h2><ol><li>Can a reader trace each claim to the submitted account?</li><li>Does a structural check test the claim, or only the consistency of its representation?</li><li>Can the people described dispute the interpretation and decide what happens next?</li></ol><p>A readable report can still encode a weak or inappropriate model. Human review must address the interpretation as well as the quotations.</p></section>'
page('/reading/orglens/','OrgLens: readable reports and the limits of their evidence',body)
body='<p>A systems map makes selections: what matters, what belongs together, what came before, and what a connection means. The Necessary Tangle treats those selections as claims that readers should be able to inspect and challenge.</p>'
for title,text in P['principles']:body+='<section><h2>'+E(title)+'</h2><p>'+E(text)+'</p></section>'
body+='<section><h2>Sources for these editorial principles</h2><p>These principles are the atlas’s editorial commitments, informed by the following discussions. They do not adopt every historical judgement made in those sources.</p><ul>'+''.join('<li>'+link(r['url'],r['title'])+'</li>' for r in P['principle_sources'])+'</ul><p>'+link('/prior-maps/review-2026-10/','Inspect the inheritance and its unresolved questions')+' · '+link('/#view=map','Explore the map')+'</p></section>'
page('/prior-maps/principles/','Principles for a revisable map',body)
